<DocsLayout title="Context Optimization">
    <h1>Context Optimization</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Cut your agent's token bill by 97%. From $2.25/request to $0.01 — same correct answer, full provenance.
    </p>

    <div class="callout callout-success">
        <strong>The problem:</strong> OpenAI charges $15/M tokens for GPT-4o. Anthropic charges $15/M for Claude Sonnet. Google charges $10/M for Gemini. Your agents stuff 150K+ tokens of context into every request — and 95% of it is irrelevant. NocturnusAI's Context Management Engine fixes this.
    </div>

    <hr />

    <h2 id="how-it-works">How It Works</h2>
    <p>Instead of dumping your entire knowledge base into every LLM prompt, you tell NocturnusAI <strong>what your agent needs to know</strong>. The engine uses backward chaining to trace exactly which facts matter, ranks them by salience, catches contradictions, and returns a minimal context window.</p>

    <ol>
        <li><strong>Goal resolution</strong> — backward chaining traces which facts are relevant to your question</li>
        <li><strong>Salience ranking</strong> — facts scored by recency, frequency, and priority</li>
        <li><strong>Contradiction detection</strong> — conflicting facts flagged or auto-resolved before reaching the LLM</li>
        <li><strong>Deduplication</strong> — cross-source duplicates merged</li>
        <li><strong>Token-optimized output</strong> — minimal context window with full provenance</li>
    </ol>

    <p>The entire pipeline runs in under 50ms.</p>

    <hr />

    <h2 id="quickstart">Quick Start — HTTP API</h2>
    <p>Assumes you have a running NocturnusAI server with some facts loaded. See <a href={`${base}/docs`}>Quickstart</a> to get set up.</p>

    <h3>1. Optimize context for a goal</h3>
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl -X POST http://localhost:9300/context/optimize \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Tenant-ID: default" \
  -d '&#123;
    "goals": [
      &#123;"predicate": "eligible_for_sla", "args": ["acme_corp"]&#125;
    ],
    "maxFacts": 25,
    "sessionId": "session-1"
  &#125;'</code></pre>

    <p><strong>Response:</strong> 15 goal-relevant facts, ~820 tokens, full provenance chains.</p>
    <pre><code class="language-json">&#123;
  "windowId": "ctx-a7f3b2e1",
  "totalFactsAvailable": 512,
  "totalFactsIncluded": 15,
  "totalCharCount": 820,
  "goalDriven": true,
  "contradictionsFound": 1,
  "contradictionsResolved": 1,
  "entries": [
    &#123;
      "predicate": "eligible_for_sla",
      "args": ["acme_corp"],
      "salience": 0.98,
      "category": "goal_relevant",
      "provenance": &#123;
        "rule": "eligible_for_sla(?c) :- customer_tier(?c, enterprise)",
        "premises": ["customer_tier(acme_corp, enterprise)"]
      &#125;
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>

    <div class="not-prose my-6 p-4 bg-slate-900 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-slate-300">
        <strong>The math:</strong> 512 facts × ~300 chars = ~150K tokens = <strong>$2.25 at $15/M</strong>. After optimization: 820 tokens = <strong>$0.01</strong>. That's a 97% cost reduction per request.
    </div>

    <h3>2. Get incremental diffs (multi-turn)</h3>
    <p>On subsequent turns, send the same <code>sessionId</code> to get only what changed:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl -X POST http://localhost:9300/context/diff \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Tenant-ID: default" \
  -d '&#123;
    "sessionId": "session-1",
    "goals": [&#123;"predicate": "eligible_for_sla", "args": ["acme_corp"]&#125;]
  &#125;'</code></pre>

    <p>Returns only added/removed facts since the last call — further reducing token spend.</p>

    <h3>3. Ingest + optimize in one call</h3>
    <p>Extract facts from text and get an optimized context window back in a single request:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl -X POST http://localhost:9300/context/ingest \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Tenant-ID: default" \
  -d '&#123;
    "text": "Acme Corp signed a $2M contract with an arbitration clause.",
    "goals": [&#123;"predicate": "enforceable", "args": ["contract_001"]&#125;],
    "maxFacts": 25
  &#125;'</code></pre>

    <hr />

    <h2 id="python">Python SDK</h2>
    <pre><code class="language-python">from nocturnusai import SyncNocturnusAIClient

client = SyncNocturnusAIClient("http://localhost:9300")

# Goal-driven optimization
ctx = client.optimize_context(
    goals=[&#123;"predicate": "eligible_for_sla", "args": ["acme_corp"]&#125;],
    max_facts=25,
    session_id="session-1"
)
print(f"&#123;ctx.total_facts_included&#125; facts, &#123;ctx.total_char_count&#125; chars")
# 15 facts, 820 chars — vs. 150K unoptimized

# Feed optimized context to your LLM
context_text = "\n".join(
    f"&#123;e.predicate&#125;(&#123;', '.join(e.args)&#125;)" for e in ctx.entries
)
# Pass context_text to OpenAI/Claude/Gemini — 97% fewer tokens billed</code></pre>

    <hr />

    <h2 id="openai">With OpenAI (GPT-4o)</h2>
    <p>Here's the full pattern: use NocturnusAI to optimize context, then pass only the relevant facts to GPT-4o. This is where you save $2.24 per request.</p>

    <pre><code class="language-python">import openai
from nocturnusai import SyncNocturnusAIClient

nocturnus = SyncNocturnusAIClient("http://localhost:9300")
oai = openai.OpenAI()

# Step 1: Get optimized context (820 tokens instead of 150K)
ctx = nocturnus.optimize_context(
    goals=[&#123;"predicate": "eligible_for_sla", "args": ["acme_corp"]&#125;],
    max_facts=25
)

# Step 2: Build a minimal system prompt from optimized facts
facts = "\n".join(f"- &#123;e.predicate&#125;(&#123;', '.join(e.args)&#125;)" for e in ctx.entries)
rules = "\n".join(f"- &#123;r&#125;" for r in ctx.relevant_rules)

system_prompt = f"""You are a contract analysis agent.
Answer based ONLY on these verified facts:

Facts:
&#123;facts&#125;

Rules:
&#123;rules&#125;

Contradictions found: &#123;ctx.contradictions_found&#125;
"""

# Step 3: Call GPT-4o with optimized context
response = oai.chat.completions.create(
    model="gpt-4o",
    messages=[
        &#123;"role": "system", "content": system_prompt&#125;,
        &#123;"role": "user", "content": "Is contract_001 enforceable?"&#125;
    ]
)

print(response.choices[0].message.content)
# Correct answer, sourced from verified facts
# Billed: ~1,200 tokens instead of ~152,000</code></pre>

    <div class="not-prose my-6 p-4 bg-slate-900 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-slate-300">
        <strong>Cost at scale:</strong> 1,000 requests/hour × 24 hours × 30 days:
        <ul style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem;">
            <li><strong>Without NocturnusAI:</strong> 150K tokens × $15/M = $2.25/req → <strong>$54,000/month</strong></li>
            <li><strong>With NocturnusAI:</strong> 1.2K tokens × $15/M = $0.018/req → <strong>$432/month</strong></li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <h2 id="anthropic">With Claude (Anthropic)</h2>
    <p>Same pattern, different provider. Same savings.</p>

    <pre><code class="language-python">import anthropic
from nocturnusai import SyncNocturnusAIClient

nocturnus = SyncNocturnusAIClient("http://localhost:9300")
claude = anthropic.Anthropic()

# Optimized context — 820 tokens instead of 150K
ctx = nocturnus.optimize_context(
    goals=[&#123;"predicate": "eligible_for_sla", "args": ["acme_corp"]&#125;],
    max_facts=25
)

facts = "\n".join(f"- &#123;e.predicate&#125;(&#123;', '.join(e.args)&#125;)" for e in ctx.entries)

response = claude.messages.create(
    model="claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
    max_tokens=1024,
    system=f"Answer based ONLY on these verified facts:\n&#123;facts&#125;",
    messages=[&#123;"role": "user", "content": "Is Acme Corp eligible for SLA support?"&#125;]
)

print(response.content[0].text)
# $0.01 instead of $2.25. Same correct answer.</code></pre>

    <hr />

    <h2 id="langchain">With LangChain</h2>
    <p>Use the NocturnusAI LangChain tools — context optimization is built into the <code>nocturnusai_context</code> tool.</p>

    <pre><code class="language-python">from nocturnusai import SyncNocturnusAIClient
from nocturnusai.langchain import get_nocturnusai_tools
from langchain_anthropic import ChatAnthropic
from langchain.agents import AgentExecutor, create_tool_calling_agent
from langchain_core.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate

client = SyncNocturnusAIClient("http://localhost:9300")
tools = get_nocturnusai_tools(client)

llm = ChatAnthropic(model="claude-sonnet-4-20250514")
prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([
    ("system", "You have access to a verified knowledge base. "
               "Use the nocturnusai_context tool to get optimized, "
               "goal-relevant facts before answering questions. "
               "This saves 97% on token costs."),
    ("human", "&#123;input&#125;"),
    ("placeholder", "&#123;agent_scratchpad&#125;"),
])

agent = create_tool_calling_agent(llm, tools, prompt)
executor = AgentExecutor(agent=agent, tools=tools)

result = executor.invoke(&#123;
    "input": "Is Acme Corp eligible for premium SLA?"
&#125;)
# Agent uses optimized context automatically</code></pre>

    <hr />

    <h2 id="mcp">With MCP (Cursor, Claude Desktop)</h2>
    <p>MCP-connected agents get context optimization via the <code>context</code> tool automatically. Just configure the connection:</p>

    <pre><code class="language-json">// .cursor/mcp.json
&#123;
  "mcpServers": &#123;
    "nocturnus": &#123;
      "url": "http://localhost:9300/mcp/sse"
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>

    <p>Then ask your agent: <em>"Use the context tool to get the most relevant facts about Acme Corp's SLA eligibility, then answer whether they qualify."</em></p>
    <p>The MCP <code>context</code> tool returns salience-ranked facts — the same optimization pipeline, zero code required.</p>

    <hr />

    <h2 id="advanced">Advanced Features</h2>

    <h3>Relevance Buckets</h3>
    <p>Allocate token budget across domains to ensure diverse coverage:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-json">&#123;
  "goals": [&#123;"predicate": "enforceable", "args": ["contract_001"]&#125;],
  "relevanceBuckets": [
    &#123; "name": "contract", "predicates": ["contract_type", "contract_value"], "maxFacts": 8 &#125;,
    &#123; "name": "legal", "predicates": ["enforceable", "statute_of_frauds"], "maxFacts": 10 &#125;,
    &#123; "name": "parties", "predicates": ["signatory", "witness"], "maxFacts": 5 &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>

    <h3>Diversity Caps</h3>
    <p>Prevent any single predicate from dominating the context window:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-json">&#123;
  "maxFacts": 25,
  "maxFactsPerPredicate": 5
&#125;</code></pre>

    <h3>Contradiction Handling</h3>
    <p>By default, contradictions are auto-resolved (higher salience wins). Set <code>autoResolveContradictions: false</code> to get them flagged in the response instead:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-json">&#123;
  "autoResolveContradictions": false
&#125;

// Response includes:
"contradictions": [
  &#123;
    "predicate": "contract_status",
    "args": ["contract_001", "active"],
    "positiveSalience": 0.7,
    "negativeSalience": 0.3
  &#125;
]</code></pre>

    <h3>Knowledge Base Summary</h3>
    <p>Get an overview before optimizing — useful for dashboards and monitoring:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl -X POST http://localhost:9300/context/summary \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Tenant-ID: default" \
  -d '&#123;&#125;'</code></pre>

